<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swabian Jura</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Swabian Alb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swabian Jura, or Swabian Alb, is a limestone upland in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, running about 200 km from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-forest">Black Forest</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nordlinger-ries">Ries crater</a>. Its steep northern edge was crowned by medieval castles such as Hohenzollern, Teck and Helfenstein, seats of noble families, while imperial towns such as Reutlingen grew at its foot.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swabian-jura.jpg" alt="Swabian Jura" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thoroe · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schw%C3%A4bische_Alb_-_Deutsche_Mittelgebirge,_Serie_A-de.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
